JOINS in SQL

Joins are used to combine data from multiple tables based on a related column.

TYPE OF JOINS

1️⃣ INNER JOIN
🔹Returns only matching rows from both tables.

2️⃣ LEFT JOIN (LEFT OUTER JOIN)
🔹All rows from the left table
🔹Matching rows from the right table
🔹NULL if no match

3️⃣ RIGHT JOIN (RIGHT OUTER JOIN)
🔹All rows from the right table
🔹Matching rows from the left table

4️⃣ FULL JOIN (FULL OUTER JOIN)
🔹All rows from both tables
🔹NULL where there is no match

EXAMPLE:

USE market_star_schema;

-- INNER JOIN
SELECT * FROM cust_dimen cd
INNER JOIN market_fact_full mff
ON cd.cust_id=mff.cust_id;

